From 5c354436d29e04dd7b6724fc71b5d2ac510e9158 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: krics <krics@localhost>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 20:48:45 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 2/6] qualcommax: uniphy: fix 2500base-x channel setup for
 fixed links

For 2500base-x the channel negotiates on its own even when phylink has
a fixed link, so UNIPHY_CH_FORCE_MODE has to be cleared rather than set,
and UNIPHY_AUTONEG_MODE_ATH only applies to in-band negotiation.

With FORCE_MODE set the RTL8367S-VB trunk on the TP-Link Archer AX55 v1
comes up at 2.5Gbps but carries no traffic; CH_CTRL/MODE_CTRL read
0x84C/0x821 where the stock firmware has 0x844/0x820. Reverting this
alone breaks the trunk again.

Taken from Fabiano Tassotti's RTL8367D series (branch fbinerd, commit
334f21ad3f), adapted to the current file.

Signed-off-by: krics <krics@localhost>
---
 .../files/drivers/net/pcs/pcs-qca-uniphy.c       | 16 +++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/target/linux/qualcommax/files/drivers/net/pcs/pcs-qca-uniphy.c b/target/linux/qualcommax/files/drivers/net/pcs/pcs-qca-uniphy.c
index 27f6189a330167..5a22e8a8269d17 100644
--- a/target/linux/qualcommax/files/drivers/net/pcs/pcs-qca-uniphy.c
+++ b/target/linux/qualcommax/files/drivers/net/pcs/pcs-qca-uniphy.c
@@ -508,7 +508,8 @@ static int qca_uniphy_pcs_config_mode(struct phylink_pcs *pcs,
 		misc2_phy_mode = UNIPHY_MISC2_SGMIIPLUS;
 		mode_ctrl = UNIPHY_SGPLUS_MODE;
 		mode_ctrl |= FIELD_PREP(UNIPHY_CH0_MODE_CTRL_25M, UNIPHY_CH0_MODE_MAC);
-		mode_ctrl |= UNIPHY_AUTONEG_MODE_ATH;
+		if (neg_mode == PHYLINK_PCS_NEG_INBAND_ENABLED)
+			mode_ctrl |= UNIPHY_AUTONEG_MODE_ATH;
 		break;
 	default:
 		return -EINVAL;
@@ -526,11 +527,20 @@ static int qca_uniphy_pcs_config_mode(struct phylink_pcs *pcs,
 
 	/* TODO: Fix for IPQ6018 and IPQ8074 */
 	if (uniphy->data->uniphy_type == UNIPHY_IPQ5018) {
-		//set force mode for fixed link
-		if (neg_mode == PHYLINK_PCS_NEG_OUTBAND && !phylink_expects_phy(pcs->phylink)) {
+		/* SGMII+ negotiates on the channel even when phylink has a
+		 * fixed link, so forcing the mode here keeps the RTL8367S-VB
+		 * trunk from passing traffic.
+		 */
+		if (neg_mode == PHYLINK_PCS_NEG_OUTBAND &&
+		    !phylink_expects_phy(pcs->phylink) &&
+		    interface != PHY_INTERFACE_MODE_2500BASEX) {
 			regmap_set_bits(uniphy->regmap,
 					UNIPHY_CH_CTRL(upcs->channel),
 					UNIPHY_CH_FORCE_MODE);
+		} else if (interface == PHY_INTERFACE_MODE_2500BASEX) {
+			regmap_clear_bits(uniphy->regmap,
+					  UNIPHY_CH_CTRL(upcs->channel),
+					  UNIPHY_CH_FORCE_MODE);
 		}
 	}
 

From 5bd4da8f419519f464b3e510fa670f02ed35e6f3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: krics <krics@localhost>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 21:19:12 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 3/6] generic: rtl8365mb: latch the family D SerDes

Adds 930-8 on top of the RTL8367S-VB series: 0x1D12 alongside 0x1D11,
the DISABLE -> HSGMII transition, SDS1 left disabled, and a delayed
re-latch that also sets bit 8 of SDS register 2.

Without it the trunk on a TP-Link Archer AX55 v1 comes up at 2.5Gbps
but carries no frames in either direction.

Signed-off-by: krics <krics@localhost>
---
 ...-rtl8365mb-latch-the-family-D-serdes.patch | 145 ++++++++++++++++++
 ...-rtl8365mb-latch-the-family-D-serdes.patch | 145 ++++++++++++++++++
