+Subject: [PATCH 8/8] net: dsa: realtek: rtl8365mb: latch the family D SerDes
+
+With 930-1..930-7 the trunk on a TP-Link Archer AX55 v1 (IPQ5018 +
+RTL8367S-VB) reports 2.5Gbps/Full on both sides but moves no frames: the
+CPU MAC transmits, s00_p06_ifInOctets stays at zero and so does
+mmc_rx_framecount_gb, with no CRC, alignment or FIFO errors anywhere.
+
+Three things are still missing, all from what the stock firmware does in
+dal_rtl8367d_port_macForceLinkExt_set() and sgmiiNway_set():
+
+  - 0x1D12 is never programmed. Stock writes the same value to both
+    0x1D11 and 0x1D12; setting only 0x1D11 leaves the receiver hunting.
+
+  - The receiver latches on a DISABLE -> HSGMII transition rather than
+    on the value, so writing 0x0E12 into a register that already reads
+    0x0E12 does nothing.
+
+  - 0x1D78 (SDS1_MISC0) has to stay at 0x001F. The vendor HSGMII branch
+    that programs it is reached only for EXT_PORT1; EXT_PORT0 runs
+    through SDS0.
+
+The transition also has to be repeated once the UNIPHY on the SoC side
+has been up for a while, together with bit 8 of SDS register 2 -
+sgmiiNway_set() clears NWAY_EN and sets that bit, while pcs_config()
+only clears NWAY_EN. Done from pcs_config() the link latches and drops
+again within a second or two; around 25 s into boot it holds, so it runs
+as delayed work. That part is a workaround rather than a fix: driving it
+from a link event would be better, but I could not work out which one.
+
