Subject: [PATCH 5/6] generic: rtl8365mb: trim 930-8, simplify 930-9

Checked both of namiltd's suggestions on hardware.

0x1D12 is not needed: dropping the writes changes nothing, and the
register does not decode - it returns whatever background value is
written, while 0x1D11 always answers. Removed from 930-8 along with the
now-unused defines.

Bit 9 is needed, but it is the existing MAC6_SEL_SDS0: 930-7 sets it with
its own update_bits and the final one clears it again, so it has to be in
that mask. Renamed, duplicate define dropped.

930-9 now only adds the re-latch, without touching 930-8's code.

Signed-off-by: krics <krics@localhost>
